<!--
    kuna `loweredswitch linear`: a linear chain of equality tests on one variable.

    loweredswitch re-rolls a compare cascade only when it has a binary-search
    range split, because a linear chain of equality tests reads as a hand-written
    if/else-if.  clang -O2 lowers a three-case switch to exactly such a chain.
    With `loweredswitch linear` a linear chain of three to sixteen cases re-rolls
    too, when every case body is entered only from the chain and the chain head
    dominates it, and its labels print the same signed or unsigned.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 "switch-model", option `loweredswitch on|linear`.

    clang 22.1 -O2 -fno-pie -nostartfiles -static (x86-64) of

        __attribute__((noinline)) int sink(int x) { return x * 7 + 3; }
        int sw3(int x, int *p) {
          switch (x) {
          case 1: p[0] = sink(1); break;
          case 2: p[1] = sink(2); break;
          case 5: p[2] = sink(3); break;
          default: p[3] = 0; break;
          }
          return p[4];
        }
        int chain(int x, int *p) {
          if (x == 3) p[0] = sink(7);
          else if (x == 9) p[1] = sink(8);
          else if (x == 11) p[2] = sink(9);
          return p[4];
        }

    Pass 1 is the default (`on`), pass 2 sets `loweredswitch linear`.
-->
